 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "How the falling leaves fall on our\nCurved fence - how they are fallen away\nIn small clusters, scattered\nAbove and below it array.\nWhat gives them their coldness? Where ever\nWe stand in any shade of heaven,\nThey all come suddenly falling\nAnd cover us. In some place somewhere\nWe may find them drying under\nThe sun's beating beam; others,\nStill less like earth's dead children,\nNestle beneath the forest-trees' cover,",
